# Caddyfile — AgentRail public HTTPS front.
#
# TERMINATION: Caddy owns 80/443 and the agentrail.duckdns.org certificate
# (automatic via the HTTP-01 / DuckDNS-reachable challenge). AgentRail itself
# stays on 127.0.0.1:8787 — the security group must NOT open 8787.
#
# header_up Host: REQUIRED. mcp-server.mjs, bound to loopback, runs a
# DNS-rebinding guard that refuses any Host header outside
# {127.0.0.1, localhost, ::1}. Caddy forwards the ORIGINAL host
# (agentrail.duckdns.org) by default — without this rewrite every proxied
# request 400s at AgentRail. Rewriting the Host to localhost keeps that guard
# meaningful for direct local access while letting the public path through.
# (Alternative, not chosen: teaching the server a second allowed host via env —
# more code for zero extra safety, since 8787 is firewalled from the internet.)

agentrail.duckdns.org {
	reverse_proxy localhost:8787 {
		header_up Host localhost:8787
	}
}